  { id:"QA", name:"Quantitative Ability", short:"QA", minutes:40,
    questions:[
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: profit & loss", "q": "A dealer claims to sell rice at its cost price. However, he uses a weight that is 10% lighter than the true weight, and he also mixes 1 kg of husk, which costs him nothing, with every 9 kg of rice. Approximately what is his profit percentage?", "opts": ["21.5%", "23.5%", "25%", "27%"], "ans": 1, "exp": "When he claims to give 1000 g, he gives 900 g of mixture, of which 9/10, that is 810 g, is rice. He charges the cost of 1000 g. Profit = (1000 − 810)/810 = 190/810 ≈ 23.46%, so about 23.5%."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Arithmetic: mixtures", "q": "A vessel contains 80 litres of pure milk. <i>x</i> litres are drawn out and replaced with water, and this operation is performed once more. Finally, 20 litres of the mixture are drawn out and replaced with water. If the ratio of milk to water in the vessel is now 27 : 37, find <i>x</i>.", "ans": "20", "exp": "Milk left = 80 × (1 − x/80)² × (1 − 20/80). Milk is 27/64 of 80 = 33.75 litres, so (1 − x/80)² × 3/4 = 27/64, giving (1 − x/80)² = 9/16 and 1 − x/80 = 3/4. Hence x = 20."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: time, speed, distance", "q": "Two cars start at the same time from towns P and Q and travel towards each other at constant speeds. After they meet, the first car takes 4 hours to reach Q and the second car takes 9 hours to reach P. If the first car travels at 60 km/h, what is the distance between P and Q?", "opts": ["600 km", "640 km", "720 km", "780 km"], "ans": 0, "exp": "If they meet after t hours, the first car covers in 4 hours what the second covered in t hours, and vice versa. Then v₁/v₂ = t/4 = 9/t, so t² = 36 and t = 6 hours, with v₁/v₂ = 3/2, giving v₂ = 40 km/h. Distance = (60 + 40) × 6 = 600 km."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: time & work", "q": "Pipes A and B can fill a tank in 12 hours and 18 hours respectively, while pipe C can empty the full tank in <i>x</i> hours. All three pipes are opened at 6 a.m. on an empty tank. Pipe C is closed at 9 a.m., and the tank is full at 3 p.m. What is the value of <i>x</i>?", "opts": ["6", "8", "10", "12"], "ans": 3, "exp": "A and B together fill 1/12 + 1/18 = 5/36 of the tank per hour and run for 9 hours: 45/36. C runs for 3 hours and removes 3/x. So 45/36 − 3/x = 1, giving 3/x = 9/36 and x = 12."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Arithmetic: interest", "q": "A loan of ₹ 33,100 is to be repaid in three equal annual instalments, the first one year after the loan is taken. Interest is charged at 10% per annum, compounded annually. What is the amount (in ₹) of each instalment?", "ans": "13310", "exp": "The present values of the instalments must add up to the loan: x/1.1 + x/1.1² + x/1.1³ = 33,100. Multiplying by 1.331: x(1.21 + 1.1 + 1) = 33,100 × 1.331, so 3.31x = 44,056.1 and x = ₹ 13,310."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: percentages", "q": "In an election between two candidates, 10% of the registered voters did not vote, and 10% of the votes cast were declared invalid. The winner received 54% of the valid votes and won by 1,620 votes. How many voters were registered?", "opts": ["20,000", "22,500", "25,000", "27,000"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Valid votes = 0.9 × 0.9 × N = 0.81N. The margin is 54% − 46% = 8% of the valid votes, so 0.08 × 0.81N = 0.0648N = 1,620, which gives N = 25,000."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: averages", "q": "The average of 25 numbers is 40. When the largest and the smallest of these numbers are removed, the average of the remaining 23 numbers is 38. If the largest number exceeds the smallest by 54, what is the largest number?", "opts": ["72", "81", "84", "90"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Sum of all 25 = 1000 and sum of the 23 = 874, so largest + smallest = 126. With largest − smallest = 54, the largest = (126 + 54)/2 = 90."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Arithmetic: partnership", "q": "A starts a business with ₹ 45,000. B joins 3 months later with ₹ 60,000, and C joins some months after the start with ₹ 90,000. At the end of the year, out of a total profit of ₹ 1,44,000, C receives ₹ 36,000. How many months after the start did C join?", "opts": ["5", "6", "7", "8"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Capital × months: A = 45 × 12 = 540, B = 60 × 9 = 540, C = 90m, where m is the number of months C stays. C's share = 36,000/1,44,000 = 1/4, so 90m/(1080 + 90m) = 1/4. Then 360m = 1080 + 90m, so m = 4. C was in for 4 months, so he joined 8 months after the start."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Algebra: quadratics", "q": "For how many integer values of <i>k</i> does the equation x² + kx + 36 = 0 have both its roots as integers?", "ans": "10", "exp": "The roots r and s are integers with rs = 36 and k = −(r + s). Positive factor pairs (1, 36), (2, 18), (3, 12), (4, 9), (6, 6) give r + s = 37, 20, 15, 13, 12, and each pair can also be taken with both factors negative. That gives 10 distinct values of k: ±37, ±20, ±15, ±13, ±12."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Algebra: inequalities", "q": "How many integers <i>x</i> with −10 ≤ x ≤ 10 satisfy (x² − 8x + 12)/(x − 5) ≥ 0?", "opts": ["8", "9", "10", "11"], "ans": 0, "exp": "The expression is (x − 2)(x − 6)/(x − 5), with critical points 2, 5 and 6. Sign analysis: negative for x < 2, non-negative on [2, 5), negative on (5, 6), non-negative for x ≥ 6. The integers are 2, 3, 4 and 6, 7, 8, 9, 10: 8 in all."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Algebra: functions", "q": "A function f satisfies f(x) + 2f(1/x) = 3x for every non-zero real number x. What is the value of f(2)?", "opts": ["1", "3/2", "−1", "−3/2"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Put x = 2: f(2) + 2f(1/2) = 6. Put x = 1/2: f(1/2) + 2f(2) = 3/2, so f(1/2) = 3/2 − 2f(2). Substituting: f(2) + 3 − 4f(2) = 6, so −3f(2) = 3 and f(2) = −1."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Algebra: progressions", "q": "The sum of an infinite geometric progression is 15, and the sum of the squares of its terms is 45. What is the first term of the progression?", "ans": "5", "exp": "a/(1 − r) = 15 and a²/(1 − r²) = 45. Dividing the second equation by the first gives a/(1 + r) = 3. So 15(1 − r) = 3(1 + r), which gives r = 2/3 and a = 15 × 1/3 = 5."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Algebra: logarithms", "q": "If log₃x · log<sub>x</sub>(2x) · log<sub>2x</sub>y = log<sub>x</sub>(x²), then y equals:", "opts": ["9", "18", "27", "81"], "ans": 0, "exp": "By the change-of-base rule the product telescopes: (log x/log 3)(log 2x/log x)(log y/log 2x) = log y/log 3 = log₃y. The right side is 2. So log₃y = 2 and y = 9."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Algebra: maxima & minima", "q": "If <i>a</i>, <i>b</i> and <i>c</i> are positive real numbers with a + b + c = 1, what is the minimum value of (1/a − 1)(1/b − 1)(1/c − 1)?", "ans": "8", "exp": "1/a − 1 = (1 − a)/a = (b + c)/a. So the product is (b + c)(c + a)(a + b)/(abc). By AM ≥ GM, b + c ≥ 2√(bc), and similarly for the other two factors, so the product ≥ 8√(a²b²c²)/(abc) = 8. Equality holds at a = b = c = 1/3."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Number system: remainders", "q": "What is the remainder when 2²⁰²⁶ is divided by 33?", "ans": "31", "exp": "2⁵ = 32 ≡ −1 (mod 33), so 2¹⁰ ≡ 1. Since 2026 = 10 × 202 + 6, 2²⁰²⁶ ≡ 2⁶ = 64 ≡ 31 (mod 33)."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Number system: factors", "q": "How many ordered pairs (x, y) of natural numbers satisfy 1/x + 1/y = 1/12?", "opts": ["12", "15", "16", "18"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Clearing denominators: 12y + 12x = xy, that is (x − 12)(y − 12) = 144. Both factors must be positive (if both were negative, x and y could not both be positive), so each ordered pair corresponds to a divisor of 144 = 2⁴ × 3². The number of divisors is (4 + 1)(2 + 1) = 15."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Number system: HCF & LCM", "q": "What is the smallest natural number that leaves remainders 3, 4 and 5 when divided by 4, 5 and 6 respectively, and is also divisible by 7?", "opts": ["59", "119", "179", "239"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Each remainder is one less than its divisor, so N + 1 is a multiple of LCM(4, 5, 6) = 60, and N = 59, 119, 179, … The smallest of these divisible by 7 is 119 = 7 × 17."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Geometry: triangles", "q": "In triangle ABC, ∠B = 90°, AB = 6 cm and BC = 8 cm. The bisector of ∠A meets BC at D. What is the length of AD?", "opts": ["2√10 cm", "3√5 cm", "4√3 cm", "5√2 cm"], "ans": 1, "exp": "AC = 10. By the angle bisector theorem, BD : DC = AB : AC = 6 : 10, so BD = 8 × 6/16 = 3. Then AD = √(AB² + BD²) = √(36 + 9) = √45 = 3√5 cm."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Geometry: circles", "q": "Two circles with radii 9 cm and 4 cm touch each other externally, and both touch a straight line L. A third circle, smaller than both, touches each of the two circles externally and also touches L, lying between them. What is the radius (in cm) of the third circle?", "ans": "1.44", "exp": "For two circles of radii R and r touching each other externally and touching a common line, the distance between their points of contact on the line is 2√(Rr). For the small circle of radius x between them: 2√(9x) + 2√(4x) = 2√(36) = 12, so 5√x = 6, √x = 6/5 and x = 36/25 = 1.44 cm."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Mensuration", "q": "A cylindrical vessel of base radius 10 cm contains water. A solid cone of base radius 6 cm and height 12 cm, and a solid sphere of radius 3 cm, are dropped into the vessel and are completely submerged. By how much does the water level rise?", "opts": ["1.8 cm", "2.0 cm", "2.4 cm", "3.6 cm"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Volume displaced = (1/3)π(36)(12) + (4/3)π(27) = 144π + 36π = 180π cm³. Rise = 180π/(π × 10²) = 1.8 cm."},
      {"type": "tita", "topic": "Permutations & combinations", "q": "How many four-digit natural numbers have digits that add up to 9?", "ans": "165", "exp": "Let the digits be a, b, c, d with a ≥ 1. Put a′ = a − 1: then a′ + b + c + d = 8 with all values ≥ 0 (no digit can exceed 9, since the total is only 8). The number of solutions is C(8 + 3, 3) = C(11, 3) = 165."},
      {"type": "mcq", "topic": "Permutations & combinations", "q": "How many triangles can be formed by joining three vertices of a regular 12-sided polygon such that no side of the triangle is also a side of the polygon?", "opts": ["84", "96", "108", "112"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Total triangles = C(12, 3) = 220. Triangles with two sides of the polygon (three consecutive vertices): 12. Triangles with exactly one side: choose the side (12 ways), then the third vertex from the 12 − 4 = 8 vertices not adjacent to it: 96. Required = 220 − 12 − 96 = 112."}
    ] }
